total_blocking":0},"body":"**Migrated issue, originally created by Boris Zyranov**\n\nSqlAlchemy VERSION 1.2.1\nMicrosoft SQL Server 2014\nPython 3.6.3\n\nSqlAlchemy fails to detect disconnect as per http://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/latest/core/pooling.html#dealing-with-disconnects\n\n\n```\nengine_connect_str = \"mssql+pyodbc://{uid}:{pwd}@{srv}/{db}?driver=SQL Server\".format(...)\nen = create_engine(engine_connect_str)\nprint(list(en.execute(\"select * from t\")))\n```\n\n\n[(11, 'eleven'), (12, 'twelve')]\n\n... MSSQL server restart ...\n\n\n```\ntry:\n    print(list(en.execute(\"select * from t\")))\nexcept exc.DBAPIError as e:\n    print(type(e))\n    print(\"connection invalidated\", e.connection_invalidated)\n    print(e)\n\n```\n\n<class 'sqlalchemy.exc.DBAPIError'>\n\nconnection invalidated **False**\n\n(pyodbc.Error) ('01000', '[01000] [Microsoft][ODBC SQL Server Driver]\n[DBNETLIB]ConnectionWrite (send()). (10054) (SQLExecDirectW)') (Background on this error at: http://sqlalche.me/e/dbapi)\n\n\nThird call works without me having to manually refresh engine:\n\n\n```\nprint(list(en.execute(\"select * from t\")))\n```\n\n[(11, 'eleven'), (12, 'twelve')]\n\nPessimistic approach also does not work:\n\n\n```\nen = create_engine(engine_connect_str, pool_pre_ping=True)\nprint(list(en.execute(\"select * from t\")))\n```\n\n[(11, 'eleven'), (12, 'twelve')]\n\n\n```\ntry:\n    print(list(en.execute(\"select * from t\")))\nexcept exc.DBAPIError as e:\n    print(type(e))\n    print(\"connection invalidated\", e.connection_invalidated)\n    print(e)\n```\n\n    \n<class 'sqlalchemy.exc.DBAPIError'>\n\nconnection invalidated **False**\n\n(pyodbc.Error) ('01000', '[01000] [Microsoft][ODBC SQL Server Driver][DBNETLIB]ConnectionWrite (send()). (10054) (SQLExecDirectW)') (Background on this error at: http://sqlalche.me/e/dbapi)\n\n\n```\nprint(list(en.execute(\"select * from t\")))\n```\n\n[(11, 'eleven'), (12, 'twelve')]\n\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":360473